@segment 40-42 Tanaris I & Shimmering Flats II
@start-level 40
# Carried in (segment 16's carry-out): 1111 Wharfmaster Dizzywig and 1178 Goblin Sponsorship (Ratchet), 1137 News for Fizzle
# (Mirage Raceway). 209 and 669 (Booty Bay) and 212 (Stormwind) ride along until the next Eastern Kingdoms block.
@carry 209,212,669,1111,1137,1178,1949
# Prerequisites of the carried quests, handed in by earlier segments: 189 -> 209, 668 -> 669, 1108 -> 1137, 1176 -> 1178.
@done 189,668,1108,1176
# Human Mage (from the Skyborne Mage route) segment: same quests, order, hearth bind and flights as the Skyborne Druid source (its segment 17).
# Hearth: Southshore at the start (do not use it), Gadgetzan from the Gadgetzan stop on.
# Deviations from the druid source:
# - The source had no class quests in this file; no quest removed, @carry / @done unchanged.
# - All combat hints rewritten for a mage (Frostbolt, Frost Nova, Polymorph on the second mob, Counterspell, food and
#   water between pulls). Mounted: "ride".
# - The druid's training trip at Steamwheedle Port is now Teleport: Stormwind (one Rune of Teleportation), training at
#   Jennea Cannon in the Wizard's Sanctum, then the Hearthstone to Gadgetzan. The Hearthstone is ready there: it was
#   bound in Gadgetzan at the start of this segment and not used since, with Sandsorrow Watch, both Wastewander camps
#   and the pirates in between (far over an hour), and Gadgetzan is where the route goes next. Fallback if Teleport:
#   Stormwind is not known or there is no rune: skip the two steps and just use the Hearthstone.
# - No other mage teleport in this file: every other leg here is inside Kalimdor.
# Carry-out (5): 82 Noxious Lair Investigation and 3520 Screecher Spirits (both done in the next segment), plus 209, 212, 669.
# Not taken on purpose: 1180 (Gazlowe's follow-up to Booty Bay), 1115 The Rumormonger (Booty Bay), Stoley's chain 2872-2874,
# the Pozzik chain 1183-1189, Zul'Farrak quests.
# The level 42 grind stands at the end of the Tanaris part, not at the Mirage Raceway as in the plan: the animals on the flats
# are 30-35 and worth almost nothing at 41.

# ---------- Theramore -> Ratchet -> Gadgetzan ----------
FLY Ratchet @ Dustwallow Marsh, 67.5, 51.3 | You arrive on the Theramore dock. Baldruc, the gryphon master, is in the south-east of town.
T 1111 | Wharfmaster Dizzywig, on the Ratchet dock
A 1112 @ The Barrens, 63.4, 38.5 | Wharfmaster Dizzywig
T 1178 | Gazlowe, upstairs in the big building in the middle of Ratchet. Do not take his follow-up: it sends you to Booty Bay.
FLY Gadgetzan @ The Barrens, 63.1, 37.2 | Bragok, the Ratchet flight master
S Gadgetzan @ Tanaris, 52.5, 27.9 | Innkeeper Fizzgrimble at the inn. Count your Runes of Teleportation: this segment uses one and the next one three.
A 2781 | The Wanted Poster in Gadgetzan, a few steps west of the inn
A 2875 @ Tanaris, 51.8, 27.0 | The same Wanted Poster
A 1690 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle, in the middle of town
A 1707 | Spigot Operator Luglunket, next to him
A 992 | Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser, in the west of town

# ---------- Sandsorrow Watch and the first Wastewander camp ----------
C 992 @ Tanaris, 39.0, 29.3 | Ride west to Sandsorrow Watch and use the Untapped Dowsing Widget at the small pool beside the troll huts. The Sandfury trolls around it are elite (42-44): come in from the south-west, use the widget at the near edge of the pool and ride off at once. A bug may jump you when you tap the water: just ride away from it.
T 992 | Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser in Gadgetzan
A 82 | Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser. Keep it: the Noxious Lair bugs are 47-50 and belong to the next segment.
C 1690,1707 @ Tanaris, 62.7, 29.3 | The Wastewander camps east of Gadgetzan: kill 10 Bandits (41-42) and 10 Thieves (40-41). Every Wastewander can drop a Water Pouch; you need 5. One or two at a time: Polymorph the second, Frost Nova or Fire Blast one that runs.
T 1690 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
A 1691 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
T 1707 | Spigot Operator Luglunket

# ---------- Second Wastewander camp, Steamwheedle Port, Lost Rigger Cove ----------
C 1691 @ Tanaris, 62.0, 37.3 | The southern Wastewander camps, south of the first ones: 10 Shadow Mages (41-43), 8 Rogues (43-44) and 6 Assassins (44-45). They are above you: pull one from the edge with Frostbolt, Frost Nova and step back when it reaches you, Counterspell a Shadow Mage's cast, and eat and drink between pulls. Rogues and Assassins sit in stealth, so keep your back to cleared ground.
C 2781 @ Tanaris, 61.8, 38.2 | Caliph Scorpidsting (46) stands in the middle of the southern camp and walks around with two guards. Leave him for the end of the camp, when you have a level more on you. Pull the group with Frostbolt from far away, Polymorph one guard, Frost Nova the other two and back off, kill the free guard first, then the second, then the Caliph: keep him slowed with Frostbolt and do not let him stand on you. If he is too much alone, wait for other players or come back for him after the pirates.
A 8366 | Security Chief Bilgewhizzle at Steamwheedle Port, the goblin harbour on the coast north-east of the camps
A 8365 | Haughty Modiste, in the north of the port
A 3520 | Yeh'kinya, the troll next to her. Keep it: the screechers are in Feralas, next segment.
C 8366,8365,2875 @ Tanaris, 73.5, 46.5 | Lost Rigger Cove, the walled pirate town down the coast south of the port. Kill 10 each of Southsea Pirates, Freebooters, Dock Workers and Swashbucklers (all 44-45); Andre Firebeard (45) stands by the fire near the docks (73.4, 47.1). The 20 Pirate Hats drop from any of them, but not often, so you stay well past the 40 kills: good, every kill here shortens the grind at the end. Pull from the gap in the wall, never more than two: Polymorph the second, Frost Nova runners. Dock Workers are on the piers, Swashbucklers on the ships.
A 2876 @ Tanaris, 73.5, 46.5 | Only if you find a Ship Schedule at the cove (a rare find from the pirates and their footlockers): right-click it to start Ship Schedules. No schedule: press Skip here and on its hand-in.
T 8366 | Security Chief Bilgewhizzle at Steamwheedle Port
T 2875 | Security Chief Bilgewhizzle
T 2876 | Security Chief Bilgewhizzle (only if you had the Ship Schedule)
T 8365 | Haughty Modiste
N Cast Teleport: Stormwind | A training trip that costs one Rune of Teleportation: your Hearthstone is ready and bound in Gadgetzan, where you go next anyway. No rune or no wish to train? Press Skip here and on the next step and just use the Hearthstone.
TRAIN @ Stormwind City, 49.6, 85.8 | Jennea Cannon, in the Wizard's Sanctum in the Mage Quarter: learn every spell up to your level (level 42 if you are there; the level 40 ones if you have not seen a trainer since 40). Buy Runes of Teleportation at a reagent vendor so you carry 5 or more. Next trainer stop: level 44, from Feralas.
H Gadgetzan | Hearthstone, straight from Stormwind
T 1691 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
T 2781 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
L 42 @ Tanaris, 62.0, 37.3 | The grind of this segment: half a level or more by the estimate, less for every extra pirate you killed for hats. Best spots: the southern Wastewander camp (41-45, fast respawn, close to Gadgetzan) or back at Lost Rigger Cove if the hats kept you there anyway. Stay until 42 or close to it: the Mirage Raceway hand-ins that follow add about a tenth of a level, and Feralas, next, wants 42. Sell and repair in Gadgetzan before you leave.

# ---------- Shimmering Flats ----------
T 1137 | Ride north out of Tanaris to the Mirage Raceway. Fizzle Brassbolts, on the gnome side.
T 1949 @ Thousand Needles, 78.3, 75.7 | Mage quest (from Tabetha). Magus Tirth, in the huts on the east side of the raceway
A 1950 @ Thousand Needles, 78.3, 75.7 | Magus Tirth
C 1950 @ Thousand Needles, 79.6, 75.6 | "Plucky" Johnson is the chicken by the huts just east of Tirth. Target him and type /chicken; he turns back into a human. Talk to him for the phrase
T 1950 @ Thousand Needles, 78.3, 75.7 | Magus Tirth. Do not take Rituals of Power: the book is in the Scarlet Monastery library (a dungeon), so the Mage's Wand chain stops here
T 1112 | Kravel Koalbeard
A 1114 | Kravel Koalbeard
T 1114 | Fizzle Brassbolts. Do not take Kravel's next one, The Rumormonger: it goes to Booty Bay.
A 1190 | Pozzik, on the goblin side of the track
N Ask Zamek for his diversion @ Thousand Needles, 79.8, 77.0 | Zamek stands on the goblin side. Tell him to start: while his explosion draws Rizzle away, run straight over to the gnome side.
T 1190 | Rizzle's Unguarded Plans, on the gnome side: click them while Rizzle is away
A 1194 | Rizzle's Unguarded Plans
T 1194 | Pozzik
N Next: ride west through Thousand Needles to Feralas | You keep 82 (Noxious Lair, Tanaris), 3520 (screechers, Feralas), 209 and 669 (Booty Bay), 212 (Stormwind). Your hearthstone stays in Gadgetzan.
